| Abstract Class                              | Non-Abstract Class (Concrete Class) |
| ------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| May be incomplete                           | Must be complete                    |
| Cannot create an object                     | Can create an object                |
| Uses the `abstract` keyword                 | Does not use the `abstract` keyword |
| Can have abstract methods                   | Cannot have abstract methods        |
| Can have concrete methods                   | Can have concrete methods           |
| Used as a blueprint                         | Used to create actual objects       |
| Must be extended by child classes           | Can be used directly                |
| Child class must implement abstract methods | No such requirement                 |
